32. Quick Revision Cheat Sheet
WINDOW FUNCTION
→ Calculates across related rows
→ Keeps original rows


OVER()
→ Defines the window


PARTITION BY
→ Divides rows into groups


ORDER BY
→ Defines calculation order


ROW_NUMBER()
→ Unique sequential number


RANK()
→ Same rank for ties
→ Gaps occur


DENSE_RANK()
→ Same rank for ties
→ No gaps


LAG()
→ Previous row


LEAD()
→ Next row


SUM() OVER()
→ Running / partitioned total


AVG() OVER()
→ Running / partitioned average


MIN() OVER()
→ Window minimum


MAX() OVER()
→ Window maximum


COUNT() OVER()
→ Window count
33. Most Important Patterns to Memorize
Pattern 1 — Ranking
ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
    ORDER BY salary DESC
)
Pattern 2 — Ranking Per Group
ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
    PARTITION BY department
    ORDER BY salary DESC
)
Pattern 3 — Top-N Per Group
WITH ranked AS (

    SELECT
        *,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
            PARTITION BY department
            ORDER BY salary DESC
        ) AS rn

    FROM employees
)

SELECT *
FROM ranked
WHERE rn <= 3;
Pattern 4 — Previous Row
LAG(value) OVER (
    ORDER BY date
)
Pattern 5 — Next Row
LEAD(value) OVER (
    ORDER BY date
)
Pattern 6 — Running Total
SUM(amount) OVER (
    ORDER BY date
    ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING
    AND CURRENT ROW
)
Pattern 7 — Running Total Per Group
SUM(amount) OVER (
    PARTITION BY customer_id
    ORDER BY date
)
Pattern 8 — Latest Record
WITH ranked AS (

    SELECT
        *,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
            PARTITION BY customer_id
            ORDER BY updated_at DESC
        ) AS rn

    FROM customers
)

SELECT *
FROM ranked
WHERE rn = 1;
34. Data Engineering Connection

Window Functions are not only interview concepts.

They are commonly used in SQL-based ETL/ELT transformations.

A realistic pipeline can look like:

Source System
      ↓
Raw Data
      ↓
Data Cleaning
      ↓
Deduplication
      ↓
ROW_NUMBER()
      ↓
Keep Latest Records
      ↓
LAG / LEAD
      ↓
Detect Changes
      ↓
Aggregations
      ↓
Running Metrics
      ↓
Business Transformations
      ↓
Data Warehouse
